$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3 & ≈-(3-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{6}(3-\\pi )^{3} \\\\  & =0.141\\,12,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto five decimal places." 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310588 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310589 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310590 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310591 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310592 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1041 "selection" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310591 13194139534796 true] [17592186310587 1110 #uuid "48568be9-3f4b-5e63-8a0b-a2303e2a924b" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310588 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3=0.141\\,37" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534796 true] [17592186310588 1111 #uuid "6d50619a-704a-5499-85b9-5d23ec3f9970" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310589 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3=0.141\\,24" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534796 true] [17592186310589 1111 #uuid "87856dbf-902c-59be-bb7a-3a3550435861" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310590 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3=0.141\\,05" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534796 true] [17592186310590 1111 #uuid "e7a42b83-46a7-5c46-82f9-3c498e3885a5" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310591 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3=0.141\\,12" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534796 true] [17592186310591 1111 #uuid "4d34fadd-e4f3-5e16-99f6-1bcabd9d503a" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310592 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡3=0.141\\,19" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534796 true] [17592186310592 1111 #uuid "f500879d-cb34-5b3f-8d12-86e0c88b71f8" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310594 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1089 "q-126878" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1100 "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ about $x=\\pi $ to approximate the value of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡4.$ Give your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1113 #uuid "f5d85ddc-8eac-5e3b-93df-320d5221c983" 13194139534796 true] [17592186310593 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\pi .$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ f(\\pi ) & =-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(\\pi ) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(\\pi ) & =0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(\\pi ) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-1+(0)(x-\\pi )+\\frac{(1)}{2!}(x-\\pi )^{2}+\\frac{(0)}{3!}(x-\\pi )^{3}+\\frac{(-1)}{4!}(x-\\pi )^{4}⋯ \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{2!}(x-\\pi )^{2}-\\frac{1}{4!}(x-\\pi )^{4}⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=4$ into the above to approximate $\\operatorname{cos}⁡4.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4 & ≈-1+\\frac{1}{2!}(4-\\pi )^{2}-\\frac{1}{4!}(4-\\pi )^{4} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{2}(4-\\pi )^{2}-\\frac{1}{24}(4-\\pi )^{4} \\\\  & =-0.654\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places." 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310595 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310596 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310597 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310598 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310599 13194139534796 true] [17592186310594 1040 #edb/ref 1759218604545